    "## 4 - SMBH binary\n",
    "\n",
    "Here we have deactivated the TED and assume that it can be corrected. Note that flux gradients of each quarter is a results of the DKA. Nevertheless it is possible to at least see the flaring event with just a single camera.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Flare event: $A_{\\rm flux} = 0.08$ ($A_{\\rm mag} \\approx 84$ mmag), $t_{\\rm max} = 200$ days, $t_{\\rm dur} = 10$ days.\n",
    "- Sinusoid:  $A_{\\rm flux} = 0.04$ ($A_{\\rm mag} \\approx 43$ mmag, i.e. peak-to-peak 84 mmag), $P = 2.1$ year. \n",
    "\n",
    "Note that these signals are lower than what was originally suggested but they match the case of Hu et al. (2020) paper where the magnification is respectably 0.08 and 0.04 in relative flux."
